utput.\n        If the return value is a number, boolean, string, or nil it\n        will be included literally in the output. If the return value\n        is a non-map collection, it will be processed recursively. If\n        the return value is a map, it will be processed recursively,\n        calling value-fn again on its key-value pairs. If value-fn\n        returns itself, the key-value pair will be omitted from the\n        output. This option does not apply to non-map collections.\n\n     :default-write-fn function\n\n        Function to handle types which are unknown to data.json. Defaults\n        to a function which throws an exception. Expects to be called with\n        three args, the value to be serialized, the output stream, and the\n        options map.\n\n    :indent boolean\n\n        If true, indent json while writing (default = false)." _kc$1965 823 _kc$1966 1 _kc$1967 "clojure/data/json.clj")))) _kc$1968)))) (jolt-register-source! "write" "clojure.data.json" "write" "clojure/data/json.clj" 823) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "$Rapply" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "butlast" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "count" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "first" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "hash-map" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "last" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "merge" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "next" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "odd?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "seq" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 823 "seq?" #f) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 889 "-write" #t) (jolt-register-callsite! "write" 889 "merge" #f))
